1. **A power conditioning system comprising:**

a fuel cell configured to provide a first direct-current voltage;

a battery connected electrically in parallel with the fuel cell through a common DC link and configured to provide a second direct-current voltage;

a first power converter coupled between the fuel cell and the common DC link;

a second power converter, separate from the first power converter, coupled between the battery and the common DC link, the second power converter being bidirectional; and

a controller configured to:

control the first power converter and the second power converter to synchronize respective converter-side voltages with a voltage of the common DC link; and

in response to the voltage of the common DC link exceeding the second direct-current voltage of the battery, operate the second power converter to transfer a ripple-current component between the battery and the common DC link so as to suppress voltage ripple on the common DC link.

**1. An apparatus comprising:**

a fuel cell;

a load coupled to a DC link;

a fuel-cell converter electrically coupled between the fuel cell and the DC link;

a battery connected in parallel with the fuel cell through a battery converter, the battery converter being electrically coupled between the battery and the DC link; and

a controller configured to:

- control at least one of the fuel-cell converter or the battery converter to adjust a voltage of the DC link;
- synchronize an output of the fuel-cell converter with an output of the battery converter; and
- responsive to determining that a ripple-suppression condition is satisfied, control the battery converter to supply or absorb a ripple component of power on the DC link so as to reduce a corresponding ripple component in an output current of the fuel cell.

A power conditioning system comprising:

- a shared direct-current (DC) link configured to carry a DC-link voltage having a ripple component;
- a battery configured to provide a battery output voltage;
- a bidirectional battery converter electrically coupled between the battery and the shared DC link; and
- a controller configured to operate the bidirectional battery converter, in response to the DC-link voltage being greater than the battery output voltage, to exchange ripple power between the shared DC link and the battery so as to attenuate the ripple component of the DC-link voltage.
